Special Array With X Elements Greater Than or Equal X Leetcode Solution
Since it is responsible to store huge amounts of data and is capable of handling multiple requests from users simultaneously, it should be arranged properly. One can imagine a database as a brain!
Bit sophisticated and each part of the brain is responsible for some specific tasks. Similarly, Database is also designed.
Applications: – It can be considered as a user-friendly web page where the user enters the requests. Here he simply enters the details that he needs and presses buttons to get the data.
DDL: – Data Definition Language (DDL) is a query fired to create database, schema, tables, mappings, etc in the database. These are the commands used to create objects like tables, indexes in the database for the first time.
DML Compiler: – When the user inserts, deletes, updates or retrieves the record from the database, he will be sending requests which he understands by pressing some buttons. But for the database to work/understand the request, it should be broken down to object code.
Stored Data Manager: – This is also known as Database Control System. It is one of the main central systems of the database.
It helps to maintain consistency and integrity by applying the constraints. That means it does not allow inserting/updating / deleting any data if it has child entry.
It helps to back up the database and recovers data whenever required. Since it is a huge database and when there is any unexpected exploit of the transaction, and reverting the changes is not easy.
Compiled DML: – Some of the processed DML statements (insert, update, delete) are stored in it so that if there are similar requests, it will be re-used. Data Dictionary: – It contains all the information about the database.
