To be in F-1 “status” means that you are legally in the U.S. and have benefits and restrictions specified in the immigration regulations for the F-1 visa category. You gain status either by entering the U.S. with F-1 documents or, for people already in the U.S. in a different status, by applying to U.S.
SEVIS is a U.S. government database that allows schools and federal immigration agencies to exchange data on the status of international students. Information is transmitted electronically throughout an F-1 student’s academic career in the U.S.
Depart the U.S. Once you leave the U.S. (including trips to Canada and Mexico) after completing your studies you are not eligible to re-enter with your current I-20. The grace period is meant for travel within the states and preparation to depart the U.S.
Business Language Skills offers a variety of courses that are targeted to International Business Professionals. This course guides participants to effectively communicate in the target language needed in corporate environments.
Perfect the Language Skill You Need
As a non-native English speaker, it speaks to your character and abilities when you can offer advanced English comprehension in addition to your native language skills. Your willingness to go above and beyond by learning a new language shows future employers and business partners that you can be trusted to get the job done.
Contracts and technical lingo are hard enough to follow, but the formalities of business English to make it that much harder to understand. Just a minor misunderstanding could be the difference between millions of dollars or thousands of jobs lost, so we teach you to approach business English with a critical and analytical eye.
At BEI, we will equip you with the language skills you need to convey intelligence, sophistication, confidence and grace. You will learn the language tools to thrive in any environment, formal or social.
This prep course focuses on strategies for success. For this reason, applicants must take a placement exam to determine high intermediate English proficiency to be ready for this course.
The TOEFL exam can cost up to $250 each time you take it, and registration opens six months prior to your test date. In other words, it will cost you a lot of time and money if you don’t pass the TOEFL.
University Partnerships - Bilingual Education Institute
Successful completion of BEI’s Intensive English Level 7 or 8 is equivalent to the English proficiency standards dictated by TOEFL, so you can skip the test and use your certificate as proof of your English mastery with our university partners.
Your native language is NOT English
Articulation Agreements You can skip the TOEFL altogether and head straight to university!
Thanks to our Articulation Agreements with several respected schools, our Intensive English Level 7 and 8 Certificates prove that your classes from BEI are equivalent to the level of English needed to meet admissions requirements . This means that you no longer have to register, study for and pass the TOEFL exam!
