Ecotourism is defined as “responsible travel to natural areas that conserves the environment, sustains the well-being of the local people, and involves interpretation and education.”
Ecotourism deepens travelers’ sense of adventure, as it brings people to more unknown and remote places and homestays give a sense of family-life, home-cooked food and a chance to interact with the communities while also providing a living to the host families and reducing migration from these communities.
