BVS is one of the tuition-free online schools and prepares students for college, the workforce, or any other paths they may wish to take.
Its curriculum is well documented and meets Florida state educational standards. The teachers are also state-certified.
Osceola offers full-time and part-time study formats as well as home education so that students can choose a flexible study option that meets their academic needs.
On our fifth list of online high schools in Florida is the Palm Beach Virtual School. This is an accredited A-rated public school offering high-quality education online to students in grades K-12.
Brevard Virtual School is another popular online high school in Florida serving students in grades K through 12. The mission of the school is to inspire and empower students for success through an engaging virtual learning experience.
Visit MDA and Apply
MDO academy utilizes a rigorous curriculum that is approved by the state and is delivered by certified teachers who are experienced at offering online teaching. Together, they prepare students for a successful life after school whether they are going further to college or the workforce.
This wraps up the list of online high schools in Florida and I hope they have helped assist you to decide which virtual school is best for your child. To get further information on the admission process and fees, you will need to contact the admissions office.
