The scholarships are designed to attract potential students with high academic performance or from poor backgrounds to come to the UAE and enjoin in their quality education.
Like I mentioned earlier, UAE is a safe and peaceful place to stay as well as study. The locals love and welcome foreigners warmly as it’s their culture to care for others.
However, places like Dubai and Abu Dhabi are expensive to live in since it is the center of UAE but as an expat student, you have nothing to worry about.
Tuition fees are equally high for universities and colleges located here but you also have nothing to worry about, after all, the post you are reading is on the scholarships in UAE for expats.
We at Study Abroad Nations have done extensive research and brought to you 13 scholarships in UAE for expats to help curb your tuition fees. You may also get lucky and get a fully-funded scholarship to last you throughout your undergraduate, postgraduate, and graduate study.
Scholarships in UAE for Expats
The grant is fully-funded covering return flights, accommodation for one year, living costs, and research support. The grant targets scholars with strong academic performance and potential in applied research.
The Institute of Management Technology, Dubai offers scholarships to expat students who may want to pursue undergraduate and postgraduate programs.
To apply, interested students will have to submit a description of why they wish to apply for a particular scholarship and fulfill other requirements.
Emirates Aviation University is keen on assisting expats to achieve their academic dreams which is why it provides this scholarship for expat students.
This scholarship passes as one of the scholarships in UAE for expats, and with the award, international students can afford higher education at a lower cost.
Undergraduates can apply for fully-funded and partially-funded awards, one of the many requests being that students possess high academic excellence.
While the partially-funded award is in form of a 50% tuition fee waiver and is also renewable till the end of the student’s undergraduate program as long as the student abides by the eligibility conditions.
Khalifa University (KU) provides a series of scholarships to both UAE national and non-national students including her expats.
The scholarships are in various categories, fully-funded and partially-funded, thus comes with different requirements which you need to look at before applying.
All of the scholarships are renewable till the end of the student’s program at the university as long as they keep up with the renewal requirements.
The scholarship award provides a 20% tuition fee waiver along with international study packages such as tuition fees, accommodation, visa, and medical insurance.
This award is one of the top scholarships in UAE for expats and provides partial education funds while studying at the university.
This is another top scholarship in UAE for expats aimed only at undergraduate students enrolled at Zayed University.
Through this merit scholarship, students from any part of the world can enjoin quality education at a 50% reduction in UAE.
The Curtin University Women in Engineering Grant is one of the best scholarships in UAE for expats but this time only for women.
To qualify for this scholarship, the candidate must have an outstanding high school academic record in engineering or mathematics or any science subject.
This is one of the top scholarships in UAE for expats, the president’s scholarship is provided by Khalifa University and aimed to reward students with outstanding academic qualities.
To qualify for this scholarship, you must not be from UAE, have a minimum CGPA of 3.3 or higher, and be enrolled in a first-year engineering or science degree program at Khalifa University. The scholarship covers 50% – 100% of tuition fees.
To encourage and assist students in enjoying quality education, Mohamed Bin Zayed University provides financial assistance to a student who wants to undertake a master’s or Ph.D. program at the institution.
The United Arab Emirates University (UAEU) provides yet another scholarship award for expatriates, but this time for postgraduate students.
The doctoral scholarship award is designed to attract high achieving graduate students to pursue a doctorate program at UAEU on a fully-funded scholarship. The benefits of the scholarship are a full tuition waiver, monthly stipend, health insurance, and a bonus of AED 2,000 – AED 3,000.
