EDS is a group of inherited disorders that affects or weakens the connective tissue supporting the skin, joints, bone, walls of the blood vessels, tendons, ligaments, and many other organs and tissues.
Does Ehlers Danlos Syndrome qualify for disability?
However, if you are unable to work due to severe symptoms from it you will be qualified as disabled and also for other disability benefits including the Social Security Disability Insurance (SSDI) and Supplementary Security Income (SSI).
Applicants must be over 17 years old, residing in the United States, and diagnosed with a rare disease such as the Ehlers Danlos Syndrome (EDS). This award is among the Ehlers Danlos Syndrome scholarships as it is a rare disease and you can apply for this award.
Other requirements include a current transcript of grades and diagnosis verification form, an essay explaining your goals and how receiving the scholarship will help you achieve them. Scholarships are awarded based on the essays, leadership abilities, involvement in school and community activities, work experience, academic performance, and financial need.
