Such RNA often has complex structures such as stem loops or hairpins. If the secondary structure of lncRNA cannot be solved effectively, reverse transcription is prone to be unsuccessful or unsuccessful when doing RT-qPCR.
RNA template quality, reverse transcription primers and reverse transcriptase, and reverse transcriptase is the core key factor. The RNA purified by commonly used RNA extraction reagents often contains residues of alcohol and guanidine salts, which have strong inhibitory effects on most reverse transcriptases; if the optimum temperature for the reverse transcriptase reaction is low, it will not be conducive to RNA.
