Before testing, all reagents must be equilibrated to room temperature (18 to 25°C).
Take out the test card from the aluminum foil bag and place it on a flat, dry surface.
Step 2: Immediately add 2 drops (60µL) of sample buffer to the sample well.
Step 3: When the test starts to work, you can see the red color moving on the reaction window in the center of the test card, and the test result will be obtained within 10-15 minutes. .
There are 3 red lines (T1, T2, and C) in the reaction window. No matter which line appears first, it indicates the presence of new coronavirus IgM and IgG antibodies.
There are 2 red lines (T1 and C) in the reaction window, no matter which line appears first, it indicates the presence of new coronavirus IgM antibodies.
There are two red lines (T2 and C) in the reaction window, no matter which line appears first, it indicates the presence of new coronavirus IgG antibodies.
If the quality control (C) line is not displayed within 10-15 minutes, the test result is invalid regardless of whether there is a T1 and/or T2 line. It is recommended to re-test.
The test result is invalid after 15 minutes.
