eTurboNews, Inc (eTN) publishes this Internet Privacy Policy to inform you of our practices concerning the collection and use of information you provide us through interactions with this website and the other eTN-affiliated websites.
eTN collects personal information in a variety of ways, including when you register with eTN on this website, when you subscribe to eTN services through this website, when you use eTN products or services via the website, when you visit eTN websites or the websites of certain eTN partners, and when you enter Internet-based promotions or sweepstakes sponsored or administered by eTN. User Registration
Users may elect to participate in promotions and/or promotional contests that eTN conducts from time to time on behalf of its clients. eTN collects personal information in connection with user registration for and participation in such promotions and contests.
Users may elect to participate in educational programs and seminars that eTN conducts from time to time. eTN collects personal information in connection with user registration for and participation in such programs.
eTN automatically receives and records information on our server logs from your browser, including your IP address, eTN cookie information, and the website page you request. eTN uses this information to help diagnose problems with our servers, for system administration, and to examine our website traffic in aggregate.
If you elect to provide us personal information, we use it primarily to deliver the service you requested. eTN may use personal information in a variety of ways including the following:
o eTN may combine information about you that we have with information we obtain from business partners or other companies in order to better deliver products and services that may be of interest and benefit to you.
o eTN may use personally identifiable information to send notification of eTN’s or our partners’ products and services by such methods as email and/or postal mail.
o eTN may send product announcements or special edition e-letters to online registrants.
o eTN occasionally conducts subscriber and/or user surveys to better target our content to our audiences. The aggregated information collected is sometimes shared with our advertisers, however, we will do not share specific individual information with a third-party.
o We may provide personal information about our users to trusted partners and vendors who work on behalf of or with eTN under confidentiality and similar agreements prohibiting such parties’ further use of the information. These companies may use your personal information to help eTN communicate with you about offers from eTN and our marketing partners.
o eTN may from time to time share personal information such as email addresses with trusted third parties who deliver content that is likely to be of interest to the user and subject to opt-out obligation on the part of such third party.
o We may share such information where we have a good faith belief that it is necessary in order to investigate (or assist in the investigation of), prevent, or take action regarding illegal activities, suspected fraud, situations involving potential threats to the physical safety of any person, violations of eTN’s terms of use, or as otherwise required by law.
What Else Should I Know About My Privacy When Online?
Please check with those third party sites to determine their privacy policy. When eTN embeds third party content into one of it’s eTN web pages, eTN will use reasonable efforts to advise our users that they have exited an eTN operated website and are entering a third party controlled website.
Ultimately, you are solely responsible for maintaining the secrecy of your personal information. Please be careful and responsible whenever you’re online.
