Our primary expertise is in CNC turning and milling processes, but we also offer a full suite of secondary operations. These secondary operations allow us to provide excellently machined parts at a high degree of completion and help us to maintain our global reputation as a leading manufacturing solutions provider.
Among the secondary services BMG offers are a number of metal finishing processes. These processes fall into one of three general categories: mechanical finishes, such as grinding and honing; metal heat treatment, which includes processes such as annealing, for strength; and metal surface treatment.
As with coating and plating, painting and color coating are metal surface treatments primarily meant to prevent corrosion. They do, however, have a number of other purposes: control and prevention of fouling, the growth of marine life in aquatic environments; increase heat and abrasion resistance, as well as grip; and decrease solar absorption, among others.
